# Anti-Slop Policy

## Purpose

Agents must not ship plausible-but-wrong code. Slop = code that compiles, looks idiomatic, and fails CI or operator trust.

Remediation gates: `ci.mdc` (static gates), `ui.mdc` (admin anti-slop). Verification honesty: `quality.mdc`.

## Lie modes (never)

| Lie mode | Project-specific example |
| :--- | :--- |
| Wrong naming | Cryptic suffixes (`m8`, `n1`, `f1`) or legacy tokens (`BidShard`, `espx`) per `naming.mdc` |
| Charset slop | Emojis, Unicode dashes, ellipsis char, `===`/`---` banners in comments and `scripts/` echo/log (`naming.mdc`) |
| Wrong types | sqlc row field vs admin `FooDTO` `json` tag mismatch on `/api/v1` handlers |
| Plausible wrong logic | Parser budget bypass, budget invariant drift, outbox double-apply |
| Weakened tests | Green CI by removing `AssertBudgetInvariant` or chaos assertions |
| Unrun claims | Claiming `make test-alloc-gate` or `pr_fast.sh` passed without executing |
| Mock bench as SLA | Citing `BenchmarkUnifiedFilter_Check_mock` ns/op as production `/track` p99 |
| Invented artifacts | Fake BPF reports, env vars, or benchmark output under `var/load-test/` |
| Doc ahead of code | Admin flag or doc behavior with no hot-path reader; cite `deploy/vendor/antifraud_backlog.md` |
| Partial rename as shipped | Migration/UI/API field renamed (`silent_reject_enabled`) while ingestion, outbox, or reports still use old semantics |
| ML action semantics lie | Doc or operator text implies per-IP ghosting; code flips campaign PG flag or only enqueues when flag already on |
| Analytics name drift | Reports/UI still `ghost_*` while wire/CH uses `silent_reject_event`; funnels under-count silent rejects |
| Product-prefixed embed paths | Static like `ad-event-processor-track.js` / `adEventProcessorTrack` in shipped snippets (`web/src/static/track.js`, `trackEvent`) |
| Marketing in tech docs | See **Documentation lie modes** below and `naming.mdc` marketing ban |
| Gate bureaucracy | New `*_gate.sh` that only wraps existing gates, or `exit 0` when the named check failed |
| Orchestrator double-run | `pr_fast.sh` child re-invokes a gate `pr_fast` already runs (naming, `admin_web`, skip-reason scan) |

## CI and script slop

Agents must not add CI layers that repeat work without new assertions. One gate = one contract; orchestrators compose gates once.

### Banned patterns (reintroduced in 2026 cleanup - do not add back)

| Pattern | Why slop | Canonical shape |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Subset gate duplicating full gate | `check_no_legacy_naming_core.sh` re-scanned `internal/` subset already covered by `check_no_legacy_naming.sh` allowlist | Single `check_no_legacy_naming.sh` in `pr_fast.sh` |
| Doc gate calling unrelated gate | `antifraud_doc_gate.sh` invoked full legacy naming; `pr_fast` already runs naming before it | `antifraud_doc_gate.sh` = ANTIFRAUD.md vs code only |
| Thin skip gate | `integration_skip_reason_gate.sh` only checked bare `t.Skip()`; subset of `anti_slop_gate.sh` | `anti_slop_gate.sh` + `integration_test_slop_gate.sh` in `pr_fast` |
| Same static scan in two tiers | `tier_a.sh` and `anti_slop_gate.sh` both scanned `_ = json.Unmarshal` / `_ = w.Write` in handlers/outbox | Keep scan in `anti_slop_gate.sh` only |
| Hardcoded script inventory | `check_scripts_layout.sh` listed ~30 "required" paths that must exist on disk | CI/Makefile ref check + `verify_redis_topology_test.sh` only |
| Fake pass on failure | `license_red_team_garbled.sh` used `exit 0` when garble build failed | Named gate must `exit 1` on failure; optional tier uses env flag + `skip_gate`, not silent pass |
| Always-SKIP gate rows | `license_verify_tier.sh` `release-1` / `release-2` for models not in tree | Omit gate rows; document optional tooling in `DEVELOPMENT.md` if needed |
| Duplicate gate invocation | `admin_web.sh` called `selfserve_nav_gate.sh` twice | One call per gate per orchestrator |
| Matryoshka test orchestrators | `license_red_team.sh` tail-called `license_red_team_extended.sh` while `license_verify_tier` also ran extended | `make license-red-team` = red-team then extended; `license_verify_tier` owns tier matrix |
| Smoke re-running parent gates | `release_qa_smoke.sh` re-ran `license_fuzz_nightly_gate` + extended already in `license_verify_tier` | `release_qa_smoke.sh` = go fuzz smoke + `license_garbled_alloc_gate` only |
| Preflight double admin | `admin_release_preflight_gate.sh` ran `admin_web.sh` then `pr_fast.sh` (which ends with `admin_web`) | `pr_fast` **or** `admin_web` when `ADMIN_RELEASE_SKIP_PR_FAST=1` |
| Smoke before full orchestrator | `cpa_compliance_smoke.sh` called `check_ui_slop` / `report_live_routes` then `admin_web.sh` | Call `admin_web.sh` once (sub-gates live inside it) |

### License verify composition (canonical)

| Entry | Runs |
| :--- | :--- |
| `make license-red-team` | `scripts/security/license_red_team.sh` then `scripts/test/license_red_team_extended.sh` |
| `make license-verify` | `scripts/ci/license_verify_tier.sh` (baseline, crypto, entangle, release-4..6 optional, alloc) |
| `release_qa_smoke.sh` | Fuzz targets + `license_garbled_alloc_gate` only; not fuzz_nightly or extended |

Do not add a new `*_gate.sh` whose body is only `bash` lines to other gates unless it encodes a new env matrix or fail-closed contract. Prefer extending the leaf gate or the single orchestrator (`pr_fast.sh`, `license_verify_tier.sh`, `admin_web.sh`).

## Documentation lie modes (never)

Applies to `README.md`, `docs/`, `deploy/vendor/`, admin user-visible copy, Grafana panel text. Engineering tone only: paths, HTTP codes, SLA from `core.mdc`, license facts from `sku.yaml`.

| Lie | What code actually does | Write instead |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Microbench as prod SLA | `BenchmarkFilterFraudBoost` ~90 ns/op is isolated `FilterEngine.Check`; prod is full chain + Redis Lua | Name bench; E2E p99 from load test / Prometheus |
| "Reads boost in-memory under 90 ns" beside Redis | Boost snapshot is Go `atomic.Value` map; ML writer uses Redis in background | "Snapshot lookup in Go; Redis sync async" |
| "Eliminated `SISMEMBER` / `HEXISTS` / INCR" | `FraudBlacklistFilter` still `SISMEMBER`; placement cache misses `HEXISTS`; RPD uses Redis `INCR` | "Cached with Redis on miss" or implement cache first |
| "Local atomic ingress RPD" | `EntitlementsFilter` / `lua_precheck` Redis `INCR` | State Redis INCR or implement local counter |
| `silent_reject_enabled` "wired" | Only PG migration + admin PATCH; hot path ignored flag | `fraudTrackOutcome` reads registry; holdout tests; decoy 202/302 vs 403 |
| ML `ghost` / `silent_reject` action | Per-IP decoy or auto-enable campaign | Outbox adds IP to `blacklist:fraud`; does not `UPDATE silent_reject_enabled`; legacy action alias `ghost` only on enqueue |
| IVT tier ML "enforcement" | Doc implies all tiers get boost/blacklist | `FraudTierIVT` with flag off must blacklist or document no-op; suspect=boost, block=blacklist |
| L2 shadow billing omitted | "Shadow accepted, logged to CH" | State whether `UnifiedFilter` Lua ran; fraud signals before Lua skip debit when short-circuited |
| Fraud stream parity | "All fraud rejects in CH" | Silent accept enqueues fraud stream; hard 403 must too if funnels count blocks |
| `silent_reject_event` unset | Silent reject returns 202 but analytics empty | Set event flag on silent accept; CH column `silent_reject_event`; not legacy `ghost_event` in new code |
| XDP stops residential fraud | XDP drops listed L3/L4; rotating proxies evade host maps | "L4 flood + known IPs"; optional `ebpf_xdp_edge` |
| JA3/TCP MSS as client signals | Tracker reads edge headers; CDN terminates TCP | CDN disclaimer; `edge.mdc` disable flags |
| "Guarantee", "never" (ML on hot path) | OK if qualified: ML in sidecar only | "Batch only"; cite `cmd/fraud-scorer` |
| Mixed ns / us / ms in one claim | Different layers have different budgets | Table per layer: edge, local filter, Redis Lua, handler E2E |

Open implementation gaps: `deploy/vendor/antifraud_backlog.md` (semantic slugs, not ticket IDs). Do not close backlog items in docs alone.

CI: `bash scripts/ci/antifraud_doc_gate.sh` (in `pr_fast.sh`; stale hot-path text, false eliminated claims, legacy naming in vendor docs).

## Forbidden marketing prose (`naming.mdc`)

Banned words and sections in technical docs (not in `deploy/vendor/SALES.md` SKU tables): `enterprise-grade`, `premium`, `ultra-low`, `guarantee`, `hundreds of thousands`, `Why * choose`, competitor comparison tables, "crush" / "eliminates fees" pitch. Price tiers: cite `sku.yaml` only without competitor anchors.


Script: `bash scripts/ci/anti_slop_gate.sh` (included in `pr_fast.sh`).

Scope: `internal/controlplane`, `internal/ingestion`, `internal/payment`, `pkg/`.

| Pattern | Why banned |
| :--- | :--- |
| Bare `t.Skip()` | Hides missing coverage |
| `t.Skip("skipping integration test")` without `integration:` prefix | Gate cannot distinguish real skip |
| `testing.Short()` skip without `integration:` in reason | Same |
| `testing.Testing()` in non-test `.go` | Test hook in production code |
| `os.Getenv("CI")` branch in prod | Environment-specific behavior |
| `_ = json.Unmarshal` / `_ = w.Write` in `*_handlers.go`, `outbox_*.go` | Silent handler failures |
| `nolint:errcheck` without ticket | Permanent error swallow |
| `BenchmarkUnifiedFilter_Check` (unqualified) | Must be `_mock` - uses mock Redis |
| `httptest.NewServer` in package that also uses testcontainers for DB | Fake infra when real PG/Redis required |

## Integration test slop

Script: `bash scripts/ci/integration_test_slop_gate.sh`.

Every `*_integration_test.go` must:

1. Guard with `testing.Short()` and skip reason containing `integration:`.
2. Call a real infra helper (`testutil.SetupPostgres`, `SetupRedis`, `setupTestDB`, etc.).
3. Contain behavioral assertions (`require.*` / `assert.*`).
4. Never use `testify/mock`, `gomock`, or bare `t.Skip()`.
5. Never leave scaffold placeholders (`scaffold_test: add a held-out negative assertion` only).

## Hot-path static slop

Scripts: `hot_path_static_gate.sh`, `lint_go_hotpath_forbid_gate.sh`, `escape_heap_gate.sh`.

Files: `handler.go`, `handler_http*.go`, `filter*.go`, `filters.go`, `internal/rtb/*.go`.

Banned in hot request path:

- `fmt.Sprintf`, `interface{}` boxing, `context.WithValue`
- `context.WithTimeout` / `context.WithCancel` in request-path sources and `internal/domain` (except allowlisted cold broker/store files)

New heap escapes above baseline or in changed hot files fail `escape_heap_gate.sh`. After hot-path edits run `make test-alloc-gate`.

## Cold-path static slop

Scripts: `cold_path_static_gate.sh`, `cold_path_json_gate.sh`.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Redis commands | No `KEYS`, `FLUSHALL`, `FLUSHDB` in production Go |
| N+1 queries | No new O(N) DB-in-loop patterns in changed controlplane/payment/ledger files |
| Body limits | `pkg/coldpath.DefaultMaxBody=64KiB`; handlers use `ReadLimitedBody` / `DecodeRequestOrBadRequest` - not raw `io.ReadAll` |

Run: `bash scripts/ci/cold_path_static_gate.sh`; `go test ./pkg/coldpath/ -run TestReadLimitedBody`.

## Bench honesty

| Benchmark | What it actually measures |
| :--- | :--- |
| `BenchmarkUnifiedFilter_Check_mock` | Mock Redis; Go wrapper only |
| `BenchmarkLuaScript_Happy` | Needs testcontainers + `run_bench.sh` |
| `BenchmarkAdsPacketHandlerProto` | No live filter chain |
| `BenchmarkFilterFraudBoost` | Snapshot only; not LGBM |
| `BenchmarkLGBMScorer_ScoreBatch10k` | Cold path (`internal/fraud`) only |

Tracker p95/p99 SLA = load test / Prometheus (`malformed.sh`, `parser_chaos_load.sh`), not unit microbenches.

## Admin UI slop

Scripts: `check_ui_slop.sh`, `report_live_routes_gate.sh`.

Forbidden in shipped `web/src/views`:

- `(skeleton)` in user-visible copy
- "not fully available yet" / "Skeleton shows expected"
- Empty table blaming user to "connect API"
- `live: true` on route without real `/api/v1` backend
- Fetch then always empty table; `catch` -> empty with no error UI
- "Saved" toast before 2xx; form fields not in Go DTO
- Hardcoded demo KPIs; echoing secrets/tokens after save

Required: read handler DTO first; `StubBanner` for 501; `renderErrorBlock` on errors; `apiConfirmed` on mutations; `npm run typecheck`; `bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh` before claiming UI done.

Forbidden in `web/src` copy and embed snippets:

- Report catalog keys/titles `ghost-impression-funnel`, column headers "Ghost" when API field is `silent_reject_*` (canonical route `silent-reject-impression-funnel`; legacy URL alias ok one release)
- Product-prefixed static filenames (`ad-event-processor-track.js`); use `web/src/static/track.js` and export `trackEvent`
- User-visible "fixed" for antifraud flags when only admin toggle or migration landed

## Code slop patterns (no dedicated gate - still reject)

- Provider/Factory/Strategy interfaces with one implementation (`cold-path.mdc`).
- Repository interface over sqlc when `db.Queries` suffices.
- `map[string]any` JSON builders on cold path.
- Parallel Entity/Model/View/DTO for same table.
- `defer` in hot-path loops; closures capturing per-request state on `/track`.
- Dynamic Prometheus label values built per request in filter loops.
- Importing `internal/fraud` scoring into tracker ingest.
- Postgres/ClickHouse/outbox side effects inside `processTrack()` or filter `Check`.
- Hand-editing `*.pb.go`, `*.sql.go`, bpf2go output.
- Docs-only commits without code in the same changeset (`core.mdc`).
- Cold-path ML enforcement that mutates operator campaign config (`silent_reject_enabled`) instead of per-IP Redis/CH effects.
- Empty `garble_policy.go` or missing `//garble:ignore` while `TestGarblePolicy_ingestionPackageIgnored` expects it.

## Fault and chaos proof slop

- `fault_proof gap=open` without follow-up test or explicit PR waiver.
- Chaos tests that pass only because chaos pct is 0.
- Parser security change without `TestChaos_CrossHop_NginxGnet` `differential_count=0`.
- New hot-path write path without fault proof (`fault-tests.mdc`).

## Agent checklist before "done"

| Step | Command / action |
| :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Every new symbol resolves (`go build` / `go test -c`) |
| 2 | Hot path does not import cold fraud scoring |
| 3 | Paste command + package path for verification runs actually executed |
| 4 | Explain why scripts/tests changed |
| 5 | Add a test that fails without the change when behavior is non-obvious |
| 6 | Doc claims match code or cite `antifraud_backlog.md` slug; run `antifraud_doc_gate.sh` when touching vendor antifraud docs |
| 7 | Run `bash scripts/ci/pr_fast.sh` scoped to touched packages |
| 8 | Antifraud: verify silent reject path (flag, decoy HTTP, stream/CH flag, ML action) in code before closing backlog item |
| 9 | New CI script: no duplicate gate in parent + child; no `exit 0` on failed check; no hardcoded "must exist" script lists |

